          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 2 · Religious Extremism Frame\n## 2:30–7:45\n\nLionel first separates religion from what he considers unhealthy or manipulative manifestations of religion. He also connects anti-Muslim rhetoric with support for Middle East policy, then argues that audiences must hold several apparently conflicting thoughts at once. \n\n**Function:** define a distinction that will govern the first cluster of clips:\n\n`faith is not the problem -> distorted performance and weaponized religious language are the problem`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study05-seg3",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "3 · Airplane Clip as Analogy",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -600,
        "y": -100
