      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 3 · Airplane Clip as Analogy\n## 7:45–11:31\n\nLionel plays a clip of a woman preaching on an airplane and being removed after passengers report feeling unsafe. He pauses to argue that the alarming behavior comes from standing and making intense announcements in a confined aircraft, not from Christianity itself. \n\n**Function:** use one media object as an analogy and emotional primer for interpreting a later religious speaker.\n\nThe first clip is not the main target. It prepares the audience's frame.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
