        "markdown": "# 4 · Religious Threat Audit\n## 11:31–29:57\n\nLionel introduces a religious commentator identified in the transcript as Frank Turk and announces that the speaker's biblical references amount to an incitement or directive against Candace. He repeatedly pauses, disputes the repeated language of evil and demons, reverses the speaker's accusation, and applies the biblical statements back to people accusing Tyler Robinson. \n\nHe then explains the constitutional incitement test as he understands it and argues that violent scriptural language can be dangerous when delivered to unstable listeners. \n\n**Function:** convert a clip into a legal and rhetorical threat assessment.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
