        "markdown": "# 6 · Moral Contradiction Exhibit\n## 35:29–44:44\n\nLionel says he has found another clip and jumps to a discussion involving Dennis Prager and simulated sexual material. He plays the exchange, reacts to Prager's distinction between evil thoughts and evil behavior, and then expands into the difference between criminal prosecution, religious judgment, fantasy, and conduct. \n\nHe uses the passage to argue that figures presenting themselves as moral authorities often appear inconsistent or confused.\n\n**Function:** expose a claimed contradiction between public moral identity and an actual position.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
