          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧬 Observed Grammar\n\n**alarm hook -> sponsor -> establish broad theme -> introduce clip -> explain why it belongs -> play passage -> interrupt -> interpret words or behavior -> widen into analogy or biography -> extract a pattern -> jump to another source -> repeat -> synthesize clips into a cultural or political diagnosis -> promise continuation**\n\nUnlike Study 03, there is no single source timeline.\n\nUnlike Study 04, there is no single opponent or narrowly defined argument under audit.\n\nThe reusable structure is a **source queue governed by thematic relevance**.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study05-queue",
      "type": "markdown",
