      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎙️ Commentary Roles Observed\n\nStudy 05 expands the commentary-role vocabulary:\n\n- **primes interpretation with an analogy**\n- **assesses threat or incitement**\n- **reverses a moral accusation**\n- **applies a speaker's rule back to the speaker**\n- **disclaims source language while preserving it as evidence**\n- **reads emotional instability from performance**\n- **contrasts personas**\n- **identifies moral contradiction**\n- **audits coherence**\n- **comments on facial expression or body language**\n- **supplies extensive biographical setup**\n- **detects a subject change**\n- **extracts a common pattern across unrelated clips**\n\nThe same `Lionel Comments on Media` type remains plausible, but Study 05 makes `commentaryRole`, `targetAspect`, and `sourceQueueId` essential.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
