      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🌉 Bridge Types Between Clips\n\nThe transitions are not ordinary chapter changes. Lionel links sources through several bridge operations:\n\n- **analogy**: airplane preaching prepares the religious-threat clip\n- **shared behavior**: angry online feud supports a claim about loss of control\n- **shared hypocrisy**: Prager joins the religious-authority theme\n- **shared incoherence**: Beck, Cuomo, and others become examples of confused public commentary\n- **shared policy boundary**: the Stewart and Fetterman clip crystallizes the Israel theme\n- **persona contrast**: unstable or performative speakers are contrasted with Candace\n- **escalation**: each new clip is presented as even stranger than the previous one\n\nThese bridges may deserve semantic edges rather than nodes.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study05-production",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Live Production and Serial Continuation",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1780,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 640,
