      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-multi-clip-roundup-study-05"
        },
        "markdown": "# 📏 Confidence and Next Test\n\n## High confidence\n- Study 05 is a distinct queue-led composition\n- the multi-topic roundup format is real\n- clip order and planned queue order can differ\n- source-to-source bridges are structurally important\n- continuation state is necessary for unfinished live episodes\n- coherence auditing and persona comparison recur across multiple clips\n\n## Medium confidence\n- `Curated Media Mosaic` is the best final template name\n- Media Queue should be a visible node rather than hidden episode metadata\n- cross-clip pattern extraction deserves its own Lionel class\n\n## Next useful specimen\nA second roundup should test whether Lionel usually begins with one dominant theme, how many clips are typically queued, whether deferred topics are actually resumed, and whether the same bridge types recur.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786057401824,
